{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"862335a95925ff8add325fc95a77bc20247cdea2acd3ab917b42d6aac84b2cf9","digest":{"component_or_area":"tickets store","key_entities":["rebar._commands.compact_trigger.maybe_compact","compact_txn._compact_locked","rebar._store.sync._union_merge","*.archived","*.write.lock",".tmp-event-*","compact.trigger","intent journal","SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT","git ls-files","git status --porcelain","rebar fsck","rebar doctor --repair","rebar compact-all","--include-archived"],"problem_keywords":["wedge","crash-atomic","compaction","git merge","tracked markers","self-healing sync","fsck","doctor repair","active-only scan"],"propositions":["Compaction fold mutates worktree before git commit with no rollback on worker death, leaving dirty tree that breaks merge and strands local commits.","Git merge aborts on two variants: untracked files origin wants to create and tracked-file deletions/modifications, both unhandled and leading to data-loss risk.","Runtime markers (*.archived, *.write.lock) are tracked in HEAD due to gitignore patterns added after their commit, causing persistent tracked dirt on routine marker churn.","Compaction fold must become crash-atomic using an intent journal outside the worktree with rollback recovery preamble detecting abandoned partial folds and reverting them.","Store-wide scans (fsck, compact-all) must default to active tickets only with --include-archived flag to reach archived ones, scaling cost to active working set."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787543182935058001,"uuid":"033f30cd-a1e1-49fe-b4ca-048c9d5e7ccd"}